{
  "results": [
    {
      "n": "G1",
      "evidence": "All five screenshots show the 3D scene rendered cleanly in Chrome with no blank screen or errors.",
      "pass": true
    },
    {
      "n": "G2",
      "evidence": "Screenshots 2–5 show orbiting and zooming via OrbitControls, and the code sets maxPolarAngle = Math.PI * 0.465 and maxDistance = 15.5, preventing the camera from going below ground or outside the 34x34 tablecloth.",
      "pass": true
    },
    {
      "n": "G3",
      "evidence": "The scene uses moderate vertex counts (~60k total triangles), instanced sugar meshes, two shadow maps (2048 and 1024), and lightweight post-processing (UnrealBloomPass and BokehPass), which easily runs at 30+ fps on a standard laptop.",
      "pass": true
    },
    {
      "n": "1",
      "evidence": "All screenshots show an on-screen UI bar (#ui) at the bottom with text ('Drag to orbit · Scroll to zoom') and two interactive buttons ('Macro DoF: ON' and 'Hero Angle').",
      "pass": false
    },
    {
      "n": "2",
      "evidence": "In the animate() function, only camera controls and depth-of-field focus distance are updated; there is no environmental motion running in the scene.",
      "pass": false
    },
    {
      "n": "3",
      "evidence": "Screenshot 1 matches the reference photo's camera angle and framing: close up, slightly elevated, with the stack of French toast centered on the dark plate.",
      "pass": true
    },
    {
      "n": "4",
      "evidence": "Screenshots 1–3 and 5 clearly show three slices of French toast stacked and rotated at slight offsets, matching the photo.",
      "pass": true
    },
    {
      "n": "5",
      "evidence": "Screenshots 1–4 show banana slices placed between the toast layers, on top, and resting on the plate around the stack.",
      "pass": true
    },
    {
      "n": "6",
      "evidence": "Screenshots 1–5 show a cluster of blueberries on top of the stack and additional blueberries scattered around the base on the plate.",
      "pass": true
    },
    {
      "n": "7",
      "evidence": "Screenshots 1 and 5 show the stack sitting on a dark round plate resting on a grey-brown cloth surface.",
      "pass": true
    },
    {
      "n": "8",
      "evidence": "Screenshots 1 and 4 show white powdered sugar specks dusted across the dark plate and lightly over the toast and berries.",
      "pass": true
    },
    {
      "n": "9",
      "evidence": "In screenshots 1–4, the toast slices have uniform, repetitive fluted ridges around the perimeter like scalloped crackers or tart shells rather than natural bread slices with rounded crusts and soft cut edges.",
      "pass": false
    },
    {
      "n": "10",
      "evidence": "Screenshots 1 and 4 show round banana discs with a faint brownish three-pointed seeded pattern in the center.",
      "pass": true
    },
    {
      "n": "11",
      "evidence": "Screenshots 1–4 show plump round blueberries of varying sizes with sculpted star-shaped calyx crowns at the top.",
      "pass": true
    },
    {
      "n": "12",
      "evidence": "In screenshot 1 and 5, some powdered sugar specks hover in mid-air to the upper right of the top toast slice, and the toast slices intersect heavily with the fruit rather than resting naturally on them.",
      "pass": false
    },
    {
      "n": "13",
      "evidence": "In screenshot 5 (zoomed out) and screenshots 1–3, the background behind the narrow cloth strip is a stark black void with a hard horizontal edge across the upper frame, though the stack and plate themselves are closed meshes.",
      "pass": false
    },
    {
      "n": "14",
      "evidence": "In screenshot 1 and keyLight.position.set(-5.2, 8.4, 5.4), the main window light comes from the front-left rather than behind and to the left, leaving the front brightly lit instead of backlit like the photo.",
      "pass": false
    },
    {
      "n": "15",
      "evidence": "In screenshot 1, despite BokehPass being enabled, the back rim of the plate and the horizon edge of the cloth remain fairly crisp rather than softly blurred out as in the reference photo.",
      "pass": false
    },
    {
      "n": "16",
      "evidence": "Screenshots 1, 3, and 5 show soft shadows under the plate rim, toast layers, and blueberries grounding the elements.",
      "pass": true
    },
    {
      "n": "17",
      "evidence": "In screenshots 1, 2, 3, and 5, the entire upper background above the tablecloth horizon is pure, flat black.",
      "pass": false
    },
    {
      "n": "18",
      "evidence": "In screenshots 1 and 5, the syrup drips on the toast crust look like dark, semi-opaque brown plastic tubes and the puddles on the plate look like flat reddish-brown shapes, lacking bright translucent amber highlights.",
      "pass": false
    },
    {
      "n": "19",
      "evidence": "In screenshots 1–4, the toast faces are smooth, uniform pale yellow-orange gradients and the sides are smooth plastic-like brown ridges, with no visible porous bread crumb or realistic uneven caramelisation.",
      "pass": false
    },
    {
      "n": "20",
      "evidence": "Screenshots 1–4 show blueberries with a mottled dusty blue-grey bloom texture and soft specular highlights.",
      "pass": true
    },
    {
      "n": "21",
      "evidence": "In screenshots 1–4, the banana slices look opaque, flat, and chalky/greyish, with dark shading artifacts around their rims rather than moist, slightly translucent fruit.",
      "pass": false
    },
    {
      "n": "22",
      "evidence": "In screenshots 1–5, the plate shows a dark ceramic sheen (though interrupted by a harsh circular ring line on its floor), while the cloth in screenshot 5 looks like a blurry, smeared grey plane rather than woven fabric.",
      "pass": false
    },
    {
      "n": "23",
      "evidence": "Screenshot 5 confirms that the plate and tablecloth sit level horizontally with no unintended tilt.",
      "pass": true
    },
    {
      "n": "24",
      "evidence": "Inspecting the code (addCrustSyrupRivulets and animate()), the syrup meshes are static TubeGeometry objects with no animation.",
      "pass": false
    },
    {
      "n": "25",
      "evidence": "Neither the screenshots nor the HTML source contain any steam or warm haze particle system or shader.",
      "pass": false
    },
    {
      "n": "26",
      "evidence": "There is no environmental motion implemented in the animate() loop.",
      "pass": false
    },
    {
      "n": "27",
      "evidence": "Screenshots 1 and 4 and the code (createBlueberry and createBananaSlice with per-item seeds and varied rotations/radii) show varied sizes and orientations so adjacent berries and banana slices do not look like identical copies.",
      "pass": true
    },
    {
      "n": "28",
      "evidence": "Screenshots 1–4 show severe clipping throughout: banana slices on top and between layers intersect directly through the toast meshes, and blueberries in screenshot 2 clip into the middle toast slice.",
      "pass": false
    },
    {
      "n": "29",
      "evidence": "In screenshots 1–5, the sugar on the plate appears as large, distinct, hard-edged white dots/pebbles rather than fine powdered sugar.",
      "pass": false
    },
    {
      "n": "30",
      "evidence": "Screenshot 1 looks distinctly like stylized 3D computer graphics—with scalloped plastic-looking toast, clipping geometry, coarse white dots for sugar, and an on-screen UI bar—and could not pass for the reference photo.",
      "pass": false
    }
  ]
}
